  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Terrapin**: rare: 6 archived performances [7]\n- **Oteil Horning**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Eyes**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n- **Weirwolves Of London**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [7]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **deadco2019-10-31.DeadCo2019-10-31MSG** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 192 min [1]\n- **deadco2019-10-31.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: source not stated; 20 songs; 194 min; rated 5/5 by 4 [2]. Said about its sound: Reviewer describes the recording as clean and good-sounding [4]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Travitz taped from the back of the pit [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **deadco2019-10-31.DeadCo2019-10-31MSG**: taped by JT/NY; transferred by JT/NY; source: Aud > Nakamichi CM700's W 701's > GAKable's > Sound Devices 722 @ 24/96 [1]. Also: Edited and tracked in Sound Forge Pro 10.0, then converted to FLAC with Traders Little Helper [1]\n- **deadco2019-10-31.travitz.schoepsMK4v.flac16**: taped by Jeff Travitz; transferred by Keith Litzenberger; source: Schoeps MK4V's>KCY 250/5i>Schoeps VMS5u>Sound Devices 744t [2]. Also: Fades and level adjustments in Sound Forge Pro 13, tracks split in CDWAV, FLAC made with Trader's Little Helper; Reviewer notes the recording was available the day after the show [2][5]",
